[ti:TorchNeuron: PyTorch Meets AWS Trainium]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: What if moving a PyTorch training loop to a different AI chip took one device change?
[00:00.00]Ava：如果只改一个设备设置，就能把 PyTorch 训练循环迁移到另一种 AI 芯片上呢？
[00:05.72]That could save a lot of engineering time.
[00:05.72]那能省下大量工程时间。
[00:08.89]Brian: That's the promise behind TorchNeuron.
[00:08.89]Brian：这正是 TorchNeuron 的目标。
[00:11.65]It makes AWS Trainium, a family of chips for AI training and inference, a native PyTorch device.
[00:11.65]它让用于 AI 训练和推理的 AWS Trainium 芯片成为 PyTorch 原生设备。
[00:18.96]Ava: Why does native support matter? People have already been running models on Trainium.
[00:18.96]Ava：原生支持为什么重要？大家不是已经能在 Trainium 上运行模型了吗？
[00:25.17]Brian: They have. But models, libraries, and training tools keep changing.
[00:25.17]Brian：没错，但模型、库和训练工具一直在变。
[00:29.91]Teams want to use familiar PyTorch workflows without adapting their software each time.
[00:29.91]团队希望沿用熟悉的 PyTorch 工作流程，不必每次都调整软件。
[00:36.42]Ava: So the cost isn't just how long a model runs. It's also the work of getting it running.
[00:36.42]Ava：所以成本不只是模型运行时间，还包括让它跑起来的工作。
[00:42.67]Brian: Right.
[00:42.67]Brian：对。
[00:43.09]The article includes the time spent making a workload work, tuning it, and maintaining it as models and libraries evolve.
[00:43.09]文章还把适配工作负载、调优，以及随模型和库演进进行维护的时间算进去。
[00:52.00]Ava: What changed in PyTorch to make this possible?
[00:52.00]Ava：PyTorch 有什么变化，才让这成为可能？
[00:55.54]Brian: PyTorch made many APIs accelerator-agnostic.
[00:55.54]Brian：PyTorch 让许多 API 不再依赖特定加速器。
[00:59.02]That means code can address a device through common interfaces.
[00:59.02]这样，代码就能通过通用接口使用设备。
[01:04.01]It also added official ways to register custom hardware.
[01:04.01]它还提供了注册自定义硬件的官方方式。
[01:08.80]Ava: And TorchNeuron uses one of those ways?
[01:08.80]Ava：TorchNeuron 用的就是其中一种方式？
[01:12.17]Brian: Yes. PrivateUse1 is PyTorch's extension point for a custom device backend.
[01:12.17]Brian：是的。PrivateUse1 是 PyTorch 为自定义设备后端提供的扩展点。
[01:17.96]TorchNeuron registers Trainium there under the device name neuron.
[01:17.96]TorchNeuron 通过它注册 Trainium，设备名为 neuron。
[01:23.47]Ava: Give me the simplest example. What does the developer actually change?
[01:23.47]Ava：举个最简单的例子。开发者实际要改什么？
[01:28.76]Brian: In the article's training loop, they move the model to the neuron device.
[01:28.76]Brian：在文章的训练循环中，只需把模型移到 neuron 设备上。
[01:33.63]The optimizer and the rest of that loop stay in familiar PyTorch form.
[01:33.63]优化器和循环的其余部分仍是熟悉的 PyTorch 写法。
[01:38.64]Ava: That's pleasantly boring. Does device-independent code need even that change?
[01:38.64]Ava：这倒是省心。设备无关的代码连这一步都不用改吗？
[01:44.77]Brian: Code already written against torch dot accelerator, PyTorch's recommended device-agnostic API, can run unmodified.
[01:44.77]Brian：如果代码已使用 PyTorch 推荐的设备无关 API torch.accelerator，就能直接运行，无需修改。
[01:53.62]That's useful when a project supports several devices.
[01:53.62]这对支持多种设备的项目很有用。
[01:58.16]Ava: Okay, the model is on Trainium. How does an operation run?
[01:58.16]Ava：好，模型已经放到 Trainium 上了。运算怎么执行？
[02:03.40]Brian: There are two main modes: eager execution and torch dot compile.
[02:03.40]Brian：主要有两种模式：即时执行和 torch.compile。
[02:08.62]Eager runs operations as Python reaches them.
[02:08.62]即时执行会在 Python 运行到某个运算时执行它。
[02:12.29]Compile captures work into a graph for optimization.
[02:12.29]编译模式则把运算捕获成计算图，以便优化。
[02:16.88]Ava: So eager is the mode where I can still print values and use breakpoints?
[02:16.88]Ava：所以即时执行模式还能打印数值、设置断点？
[02:22.10]Brian: Exactly. Python control flow works there too.
[02:22.10]Brian：没错，Python 的控制流也能正常工作。
[02:25.44]That's why the article presents eager as the natural choice for research and debugging.
[02:25.44]因此，文章认为即时执行很适合研究和调试。
[02:32.24]Ava: But running every operation separately sounds expensive.
[02:32.24]Ava：但逐个执行运算听起来开销很大。
[02:36.77]Brian: It can be.
[02:36.77]Brian：确实可能如此。
[02:37.53]Each eager operation compiles its own Neuron Executable File Format file, or NEFF, and launches on the device.
[02:37.53]每个即时执行的运算都会单独编译成 Neuron 可执行文件格式文件（NEFF），再在设备上启动。
[02:45.88]Intermediate data moves through device memory.
[02:45.88]中间数据通过设备内存传递。
[02:49.72]Ava: Is that why there's an adaptive eager mode?
[02:49.72]Ava：所以才有自适应即时执行模式？
[02:52.83]Brian: Yes. It's experimental.
[02:52.83]Brian：对，它还处于实验阶段。
[02:54.57]The goal is to reduce launch cost and create more chances to fuse operations, while keeping the interactive eager experience.
[02:54.57]目标是在保持即时执行交互体验的同时，降低启动开销，并增加运算融合的机会。
[03:04.39]Ava: Fuse as in combine several small jobs into one larger job?
[03:04.39]Ava：融合，就是把几个小任务合成一个大任务？
[03:09.20]Brian: That's the idea. Imagine carrying groceries one item at a time.
[03:09.20]Brian：正是如此。想象一下每次只拿一件东西搬运杂货。
[03:14.02]Combining trips can help, and you still get to work in an interactive way.
[03:14.02]合并几趟搬运会更省事，同时还能保持交互式的工作方式。
[03:20.04]Ava: Then when would I choose torch dot compile?
[03:20.04]Ava：那什么时候该选 torch.compile？
[03:23.44]Brian: For a stable model where production performance matters.
[03:23.44]Brian：模型已经稳定，而且生产环境的性能很重要时。
[03:27.43]It captures a graph of operations, lets the Neuron compiler optimize it, and produces a NEFF for the hardware.
[03:27.43]它捕获运算图，交给 Neuron 编译器优化，再生成供硬件运行的 NEFF。
[03:35.62]Ava: Do I have to compile the whole model?
[03:35.62]Ava：必须编译整个模型吗？
[03:38.39]Brian: No. The article says you can optimize all or part of it, and compiled work can run alongside eager work.
[03:38.39]Brian：不用。文章说可以优化全部或部分模型，编译后的运算也能与即时执行的运算并行使用。
[03:46.52]Ava: What happens between PyTorch code and that final device file?
[03:46.52]Ava：从 PyTorch 代码到最终的设备文件，中间经历了什么？
[03:51.50]Brian: TorchDynamo captures an FX graph, a graph representation of the model.
[03:51.50]Brian：TorchDynamo 会捕获 FX 图，也就是模型的图表示。
[03:57.19]AOTAutograd traces the backward graph ahead of time.
[03:57.19]AOTAutograd 会提前追踪反向传播图。
[04:01.42]Torch-MLIR and StableHLO sit on the path to the Neuron compiler.
[04:01.42]Torch-MLIR 和 StableHLO 位于通往 Neuron 编译器的处理流程中。
[04:06.97]Ava: That's a lot of stages. What's the useful picture to keep in mind?
[04:06.97]Ava：步骤真不少。该怎样简单理解整个过程？
[04:11.79]Brian: PyTorch gathers the work, prepares the forward and backward paths, then passes them through compiler stages until Trainium can execute them.
[04:11.79]Brian：PyTorch 汇集计算任务，准备前向和反向路径，再经过各编译阶段，最终交给 Trainium 执行。
[04:21.70]That's the key point.
[04:21.70]这就是关键。
[04:23.54]Ava: And how does someone select the Neuron compiler?
[04:23.54]Ava：那怎么选择 Neuron 编译器？
[04:27.32]Brian: They can set neuron as the default backend once, or name it in a torch dot compile call.
[04:27.32]Brian：可以一次性将 neuron 设为默认后端，也可以在调用 torch.compile 时指定它。
[04:33.76]The article shows both choices.
[04:33.76]文章介绍了这两种方式。
[04:36.38]Ava: Does native support reach normal PyTorch features, or just model execution?
[04:36.38]Ava：原生支持涵盖常用的 PyTorch 功能，还是只支持模型执行？
[04:42.97]Brian: It reaches familiar interfaces for tensors, neural network modules, automatic mixed precision, distributed work, and profiling.
[04:42.97]Brian：张量、神经网络模块、自动混合精度、分布式计算和性能分析，都能使用熟悉的接口。
[04:52.55]The article also reports broad operator coverage.
[04:52.55]文章还提到，它支持大量算子。
[04:56.59]Ava: Broad sounds useful, but it doesn't mean every operator.
[04:56.59]Ava：支持大量算子是好事，但也不是支持所有算子。
[05:01.33]Brian: Correct. We'll get to the gaps.
[05:01.33]Brian：没错。稍后会讲到哪些还不支持。
[05:03.50]For supported models, the article lists common floating-point types, integer and boolean types, and working mixed precision code.
[05:03.50]对于受支持的模型，文章列出了常见浮点、整数和布尔类型，以及可正常运行的混合精度代码。
[05:12.84]Ava: What about training across many devices?
[05:12.84]Ava：在多台设备上训练呢？
[05:16.58]Brian: The standard distributed APIs are supported.
[05:16.58]Brian：标准的分布式 API 也受支持。
[05:20.39]That includes DDP, or Distributed Data Parallel, and FSDP2, or Fully Sharded Data Parallel version two.
[05:20.39]包括 DDP（分布式数据并行）和 FSDP2（完全分片数据并行第二版）。
[05:29.67]Ava: Can people combine those ideas with tensor and pipeline parallelism?
[05:29.67]Ava：这些方法能和张量并行、流水线并行结合吗？
[05:34.85]Brian: Yes.
[05:34.85]Brian：能。
[05:35.16]The article describes tensor parallelism, pipeline parallelism, and combinations such as FSDP2 with tensor parallelism.
[05:35.16]文章介绍了张量并行、流水线并行，以及 FSDP2 与张量并行等组合。
[05:44.56]DTensor and DeviceMesh help manage sharding and process groups.
[05:44.56]DTensor 和 DeviceMesh 有助于管理分片和进程组。
[05:49.88]Ava: And the devices still need to exchange data.
[05:49.88]Ava：设备之间还是得交换数据。
[05:53.55]Brian: Right. Collective operations include gathering and reducing data across workers.
[05:53.55]Brian：对。集合通信操作包括在各工作进程之间收集和归约数据。
[05:59.70]Within a node, they use Trainium's dedicated collective cores.
[05:59.70]在节点内部，它们使用 Trainium 专用的集合通信核心。
[06:04.47]Between nodes, they use Elastic Fabric Adapter.
[06:04.47]在节点之间，则使用 Elastic Fabric Adapter。
[06:08.44]Ava: What if a project uses streams to overlap work?
[06:08.44]Ava：如果项目用流来重叠执行任务呢？
[06:12.10]Brian: Streams and events are supported. A stream keeps its own operations ordered.
[06:12.10]Brian：流和事件都受支持。每条流内的操作按顺序执行。
[06:17.70]If one stream needs another stream's result, you record an event and wait for it.
[06:17.70]如果一条流需要另一条流的结果，就记录一个事件并等待它。
[06:24.02]Ava: Like handing over a ticket before the next worker starts?
[06:24.02]Ava：就像把凭证交给下一位工作人员，他才能开工？
[06:27.95]Brian: Exactly.
[06:27.95]Brian：正是。
[06:28.53]There's a hardware detail, though: non-default streams share one hardware queue.
[06:28.53]不过有个硬件细节：非默认流共用一条硬件队列。
[06:34.41]They keep ordering and event behavior, but don't each get a dedicated engine.
[06:34.41]它们仍保持操作顺序和事件机制，但并非每条流都有独立的执行单元。
[06:40.42]Ava: So the PyTorch behavior is there, but I shouldn't picture a separate engine for every stream.
[06:40.42]Ava：所以 PyTorch 的行为是一样的，但不能以为每条流都有独立的执行单元。
[06:47.05]Brian: You've got it. And an asynchronous error appears at the next synchronization point.
[06:47.05]Brian：理解对了。异步错误会在下一个同步点显现。
[06:52.89]TorchNeuron tracks the earliest exception and reports it with its original context.
[06:52.89]TorchNeuron 会追踪最早出现的异常，并连同原始上下文一起报告。
[06:59.07]Ava: Suppose the standard operations aren't fast enough for one critical layer.
[06:59.07]Ava：假如某个关键层用标准操作还不够快呢？
[07:04.18]What's available?
[07:04.18]有什么办法？
[07:05.71]Brian: NKI, the Neuron Kernel Interface, lets developers write custom operators with lower-level hardware control.
[07:05.71]Brian：NKI（Neuron Kernel Interface）让开发者能编写自定义算子，更直接地控制底层硬件。
[07:13.78]Those operators can work in eager and compiled models.
[07:13.78]这些算子可用于即时执行和编译后的模型。
[07:18.20]Ava: Does that mean rewriting the entire model as custom kernels?
[07:18.20]Ava：这意味着要把整个模型重写成自定义内核吗？
[07:22.65]Brian: No. The article suggests using NKI for performance-critical pieces.
[07:22.65]Brian：不用。文章建议只在性能关键的部分使用 NKI。
[07:27.99]It also describes NKI-lib, an open-source set of optimized operators for common language and multimodal workloads.
[07:27.99]文章还介绍了 NKI-lib：一套面向常见语言和多模态工作负载的开源优化算子。
[07:37.43]Ava: There's a sine example in the article. What should I take from it?
[07:37.43]Ava：文章里有个正弦函数示例。它说明了什么？
[07:42.03]Brian: It registers a custom sine operator and its backward calculation using PyTorch's recommended autograd registration style.
[07:42.03]Brian：它按照 PyTorch 推荐的 autograd 注册方式，注册了自定义正弦算子及其反向计算。
[07:51.00]The forward and backward paths call NKI kernels.
[07:51.00]前向和反向路径都会调用 NKI 内核。
[07:54.90]Ava: Nice. Once it's running, how do I find the slow part?
[07:54.90]Ava：不错。跑起来后，怎么找出慢在哪里？
[07:59.55]Brian: TorchNeuron extends the standard torch dot profiler interface with Neuron-specific settings.
[07:59.55]Brian：TorchNeuron 在标准的 torch.profiler 接口上增加了 Neuron 专用设置。
[08:06.38]It can collect framework, runtime, and device activity in a connected trace.
[08:06.38]它能把框架、运行时和设备活动采集到一条关联的追踪记录中。
[08:12.38]Ava: Connected how?
[08:12.38]Ava：怎么关联？
[08:13.34]Profiling tools sometimes give me three timelines that don't seem to know each other.
[08:13.34]性能分析工具有时给我三条时间线，看起来彼此毫无关联。
[08:19.55]Brian: Neuron Explorer links events across those layers and back to source lines.
[08:19.55]Brian：Neuron Explorer 能把这些层面的事件关联起来，并追溯到源代码行。
[08:24.37]It also shows call hierarchy and dependency chains, so you can inspect what a stall is waiting on.
[08:24.37]它还会显示调用层级和依赖链，方便查看停顿时在等待什么。
[08:31.10]Ava: Can an engineer analyze the data without the visual interface?
[08:31.10]Ava：工程师能不通过可视化界面分析这些数据吗？
[08:36.42]Brian: Yes.
[08:36.42]Brian：对。
[08:36.70]Neuron Explorer emits Parquet metrics for operations and engines, and the built-in profiler tools can sort operations by device-side cost.
[08:36.70]Neuron Explorer 会生成记录算子和引擎指标的 Parquet 文件，内置分析工具还能按设备端开销对算子排序。
[08:46.78]Ava: Let's move from features to evidence. What has the team tested?
[08:46.78]Ava：从功能说到证据吧。团队测试了什么？
[08:52.00]Brian: They report a continuous sweep of one hundred thousand Hugging Face models.
[08:52.00]Brian：他们称持续测试了10万个 Hugging Face 模型。
[08:57.07]Based on download counts, those models cover ninety-nine point nine percent of real-world usage.
[08:57.07]按下载量计算，这些模型覆盖了99.9%的实际使用量。
[09:03.90]Ava: What did they check for each model?
[09:03.90]Ava：每个模型都检查了什么？
[09:06.67]Brian: Whether it loaded, ran forward and backward passes, compiled, and used device operators or fell back to the host processor.
[09:06.67]Brian：检查能否加载、执行前向和反向计算、完成编译，以及使用设备算子还是回退到主机处理器。
[09:15.73]They used reduced but representative configurations.
[09:15.73]他们采用了缩小规模但有代表性的配置。
[09:19.91]Ava: Does the article say every model passed?
[09:19.91]Ava：文章说所有模型都通过了吗？
[09:23.45]Brian: No. It says the team is closing remaining gaps.
[09:23.45]Brian：没有。文章说团队还在补齐剩余缺口。
[09:26.98]The supplied text refers to a graph of sweep results, but doesn't give a pass percentage to quote.
[09:26.98]所提供的文本提到一张测试结果图，但没有给出可引用的通过率。
[09:34.70]Ava: Was there testing against PyTorch itself?
[09:34.70]Ava：有没有针对 PyTorch 本身进行测试？
[09:38.14]Brian: Yes.
[09:38.14]Brian：有。
[09:38.44]The August twenty twenty-six run had about one hundred fifty-four thousand upstream test outcomes.
[09:38.44]2026年8月那轮测试产生了约15.4万项上游测试结果。
[09:45.65]Roughly sixty-nine thousand were skipped for stated reasons.
[09:45.65]其中约6.9万项因注明的原因被跳过。
[09:50.42]Ava: That's a large skipped group. What was in it?
[09:50.42]Ava：跳过的数量很大，具体包括什么？
[09:54.32]Brian: About thirty thousand came from PyTorch's own eligibility checks.
[09:54.32]Brian：约3万项是由 PyTorch 自身的适用性检查跳过的。
[09:58.71]Around thirty-nine thousand were deliberate Neuron skips, including about twenty-two thousand tied to missing native operator lowering.
[09:58.71]约3.9万项是 Neuron 主动跳过的，其中约2.2万项与缺少原生算子降阶实现有关。
[10:08.18]Ava: So those totals alone don't tell us a pass rate.
[10:08.18]Ava：所以光看这些总数，算不出通过率。
[10:12.13]Brian: Right.
[10:12.13]Brian：没错。
[10:12.54]The article says it reports pass rates against enabled tests, but these counts need their skip categories to make sense.
[10:12.54]文章说通过率是按已启用的测试计算的，但要理解这些数字，还得看跳过项的分类。
[10:20.96]Ava: Are there any customer performance numbers?
[10:20.96]Ava：有客户的性能数据吗？
[10:24.04]Brian: Deepgram reports that, in the benchmarks it evaluated, Trainium processed about sixty percent more input audio seconds per dollar than its existing graphics processing unit, or GPU, baselines.
[10:24.04]Brian：Deepgram 表示，在其评估的基准测试中，Trainium 每美元处理的输入音频时长比现有的图形处理器（GPU）基线多约60%。
[10:37.09]Ava: That's specific to Deepgram's benchmarks, then.
[10:37.09]Ava：那这个结果仅适用于 Deepgram 的基准测试。
[10:40.99]Brian: Yes.
[10:40.99]Brian：对。
[10:41.26]Cartesia offers a different example: it says its standard inference pipeline ran with minimal PyTorch code changes, leaving it to focus custom kernels on repeatedly used layers.
[10:41.26]Cartesia 提供了另一个例子：它表示，标准推理流水线只需少量修改 PyTorch 代码就能运行，因此可以把自定义内核的开发重点放在反复使用的层上。
[10:53.77]Ava: How does this connect to libraries people already use?
[10:53.77]Ava：这和大家已经在用的库有什么关系？
[10:58.01]Brian: The article describes Trainium support in TorchTitan and upstream Hugging Face libraries, including Transformers and Diffusers.
[10:58.01]Brian：文章介绍了 TorchTitan 和 Hugging Face 上游库中的 Trainium 支持，包括 Transformers 和 Diffusers。
[11:06.77]Those connections are central to the compatibility goal.
[11:06.77]这些集成是实现兼容性目标的关键。
[11:10.98]Ava: What's still missing in this first release?
[11:10.98]Ava：首个版本还缺什么？
[11:14.29]Brian: Some operators lack native lowering.
[11:14.29]Brian：部分算子还没有原生降阶实现。
[11:17.09]The explicit first-release exclusions include sparse tensors, forward-mode autograd, and dynamic and symbolic shapes.
[11:17.09]首个版本明确不支持稀疏张量、前向模式自动微分，以及动态形状和符号形状。
[11:26.18]The team says it's working on coverage.
[11:26.18]团队表示正在扩大支持范围。
[11:29.56]Ava: And what's next for availability?
[11:29.56]Ava：接下来何时能用上？
[11:32.46]Brian: The article announces an open-source public beta under Apache two point zero for October twentieth, twenty twenty-six, with installable packages.
[11:32.46]Brian：文章宣布将于2026年10月20日推出采用 Apache 2.0 许可证的开源公测版，并提供可安装的软件包。
[11:42.67]It also says TorchAO and FP8 are in private beta for now.
[11:42.67]文章还说，TorchAO 和 FP8 目前处于封闭测试阶段。
[11:47.04]Ava: Give me the three things to remember.
[11:47.04]Ava：说说最值得记住的三点。
[11:49.79]Brian: First, TorchNeuron makes Trainium a native PyTorch device.
[11:49.79]Brian：第一，TorchNeuron 让 Trainium 成为 PyTorch 原生设备。
[11:54.41]Second, eager, compile, custom kernels, and profiling give teams several ways to work.
[11:54.41]第二，即时执行、编译、自定义内核和性能分析，为团队提供了多种工作方式。
[12:01.26]Third, the testing is broad, but first-release gaps remain.
[12:01.26]第三，测试覆盖面很广，但首个版本仍有缺口。
[12:06.32]Ava: That's our tour of TorchNeuron. Thanks for listening.
[12:06.32]Ava：以上就是我们对 TorchNeuron 的介绍。感谢收听。
